A||||1||BENGAL4||ACCESS DOORS
Z||000000||BENGAL4||08-13-99||06:40 AM||||A friend of mine, who used to own an 86GT, said he was considering making access doors through the fire wall . Has anyone done this or knows of of this being done and could give suggestions or input on if this would work. The idea is good, considering the limited access to the back of the engine. BTW, he sold the car before he could do the project.  <br>
Z||000001||mrfixit58||08-13-99||07:10 AM||||I would not recommend cutting access doors in the firewall. The solid piece of metal is there to protect you from fire, vapors, and possible explosion. If, however, you decide to go ahead and cut the holes, be sure to seal all access panels with a something like Permitex gold that is used for exhaust manifold.
